# Resilience & UI Improvements Walkthrough

We have successfully improved the IT Inventory system's reliability and user interface.

## 📡 Email Resilience (Soft Match)

Real emails were sometimes being ignored because they lacked specific keywords like "onboarding". 

- **Synonym Expansion**: Added dozens of new triggers (Personel, Giriş, Kurulum, Donanım, vb.).
- **Smart Fallback**: If no keywords are found, the system now performs a "Soft Match". If it finds a Name and Email in the body, it automatically creates a request instead of ignoring it.
- **Verification**: Tested with an email containing no magic words; the system correctly identified it as a request and processed it into the queue.

## 🎨 UI Bug Fixes (Excel & Port)

- **Excel Dropdown**: Fixed a bug where the Excel menu could get stuck open or obscure content.
    - Updated `base.html` to use explicit click-based interaction.
    - Adjusted `style.css` with a higher `z-index` (2100) and smoother transitions.
- **Port Conflict**: Switched the application to port **9292** because port 9100 was occupied by a Dart service on the host machine.

## 🚀 Status

The system is now running locally on port **9292**.

- **Dashboard**: [http://localhost:9292](http://localhost:9292)
- **Email Queue**: [http://localhost:9292/requests/email-queue](http://localhost:9292/requests/email-queue)

---

> [!TIP]
> If you see a "Soft Match" in the logs, it means the system captured the data even though the email didn't follow the standard template exactly.
